From 3220a5bee3fd40fcd553974b8a106155a5c6200d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zed-patches <zed-patches@localhost>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 00:55:30 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] settings_ui, zeo_i18n: a Language page picks Zeo's interface
 language
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The ui_language setting (0177) could only be changed in settings.json. A
Language page now offers it as a picker: System (follow the desktop's
languages), every language zeo_i18n ships, each named in itself
("Português (Brasil)", read from that language's own zeo-language-name
message so a new language brings its name along), and the en-XA
pseudo-locale. Picking applies at once: zeo_i18n already observes the
settings store and refreshes every window.

ui_language becomes a UiLanguageName newtype, serde-transparent, so
settings.json is unchanged and the settings UI can give the type its own
renderer, the way ThemeName gets the theme picker. Ungrouped, right after
0177, so it touches only lines every USE combination has; settings_ui
depends on zeo_i18n here rather than in 0178.
---

